nger Lemon\",\"image_keyword\":\"ginger_lemon.jpg\",\"usage\":\"Drink as a tea, 2-3 times a day\",\"benefits\":\"Soothes the digestive system, reducing inflammation and discomfort.\",\"type\":\"Herb\",\"ingredients\":\"Fresh ginger, lemon juice, honey\",\"preparation_time\":\"5 mins\",\"video\":\"https://youtube.com/shorts/UJzkdo4spd0?si=ViOME2xJ9aI_I7UC\"},{\"name\":\"Fennel Water\",\"image_keyword\":\"fennel_water.jpg\",\"usage\":\"Drink 1-2 cups a day\",\"benefits\":\"Aids digestion, reducing bloating and gas.\",\"type\":\"Herb\",\"ingredients\":\"Fennel seeds, water\",\"preparation_time\":\"5 mins\",\"video\":\"https://youtube.com/shorts/W1kR5X63BoI?si=9MVV2c6IcdX412I9\"},{\"name\":\"Tulsi Ginger Kadha\",\"image_keyword\":\"tulsi_ginger_kadha.jpg\",\"usage\":\"Drink as a tea, 2-3 times a day\",\"benefits\":\"Combines the digestive benefits of ginger with the stress-reducing properties of tulsi.\",\"type\":\"Herb\",\"ingredients\":\"Fresh ginger, tulsi leaves, honey\",\"preparation_time\":\"10 mins\",\"video\":\"https://youtube.com/shorts/7WnEZyRFlK8?si=4874ls27t1rDryRa\"},{\"name\":\"Turmeric Milk\",\"image_keyword\":\"turmeric_milk.jpg\",\"usage\":\"Drink 1 cup before bed\",\"benefits\":\"Reduces inflammation and promotes relaxation, aiding in digestion and overall well-being.\",\"type\":\"Herb\",\"ingredients\":\"Turmeric powder, milk, honey\",\"preparation_time\":\"5 mins\",\"video\":\"https://youtube.com/shorts/Ih8ps6Ti_K0?si=GSblIS0725Ux6hxv\"}],\"summary\":\"As a 33-year-old male with a Vata prakriti, you are experiencing moderate stomach pain, which can be alleviated through specific yoga poses and ayurvedic remedies that balance your doshas and soothe your digestive system. By incorporating these recommendations into your daily routine, you can find relief from stomach pain and improve your overall well-being.\",\"doshaAnalysis\":\"The Vata dosha, associated with air and space, is likely imbalanced in your body, leading to digestive issues such as stomach pain. To restore balance, it\'s essential to focus on practices and remedies that calm and ground the Vata energy, promoting harmony and wellness in your digestive system.\"}', '2026-02-19 07:21:10'),
(46, 6, 'shoulder pain', 'Age: 33, Gender: Female', 'Moderate', NULL, '[{\"name\":\"Bhujangasana\",\"image_keyword\":\"bhujangasana.jpg\",\"video\":\"https://youtu.be/luTSRGXPEMs\",\"benefits\":\"Strengthens spine and posture\",\"steps\":[\"Lie flat on your stomach with legs together and tops of feet on the floor.\",\"Place hands under shoulders, elbows close to the body.\",\"Inhale and slowly lift your chest off the floor while keeping the navel down.\",\"Keep shoulders relaxed and gaze slightly upward.\",\"Hold for 15-30 seconds, then exhale and lower slowly.\"],\"duration\":\"5 mins\",\"contraindications\":\"severe_back_injury\"},{\"name\":\"Balasana\",\"image_keyword\":\"balasana.jpg\",\"video\":\"https://youtu.be/2MJGg-dUKh0\",\"benefits\":\"Relieves back tension and stress\",\"steps\":[\"Kneel on the floor with big toes touching and sit on your heels.\",\"Separate your knees about hip-width apart.\",\"Exhale and lay your torso down between your thighs.\",\"Rest your forehead on the mat and stretch your arms forward or alongside the body.\",\"Breathe deeply and hold for 1-3 minutes.\"],\"duration\":\"3 mins\",\"contraindications\":\"none\"},{\"name\":\"Marjariasana\",\"image_keyword\":\"marjariasana.jpg\",\"video\":\"https://youtu.be/Ov65nNSWrfw\",\"benefits\":\"Improves spinal flexibility\",\"steps\":[\"Prepare for Marjariasana\"],\"duration\":\"5 mins\",\"contraindications\":\"pregnancy\"},{\"name\":\"Sukhasana\",\"image_keyword\":\"sukhasana.jpg\",\"video\":\"https://youtu.be/ri9B8IzLXIY\",\"benefits\":\"Calms mind and posture\",\"steps\":[\"Prepare for Sukhasana\"],\"duration\":\"10 mins\",\"contraindications\":\"none\"},{\"name\":\"Anulom_Vilom\",\"image_keyword\":\"anulom_vilom.jpg\",\"video\":\"https://youtu.be/Nhw92icsQ1A\",\"benefits\":\"Improves breathing\",\"steps\":[\"Sit in a comfortable cross-legged position with spine straight.\",\"Close the right nostril with the thumb and inhale deeply through the left.\",\"Close the left nostril with the ring 